<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Putin agrees to resume three-way talks with Kyiv and Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5594b9999853c7683a5e3e5e0f04bb4b0e4097768b782defda115540928bc58</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/putin-agrees-to-resume-three-way-talks-with-kyiv-and-washington" /><summary type="html">President ⁠Volodymyr Zelenskiy ​said on Wednesday ​that Ukraine supported a US proposal for ​three-way talks ‌with Russia ⁠and the United ‌States at the level ⁠of negotiators to be held as soon ​as possible, preferably ‌no later than early November. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe, Russia and Eurasia Programme at Chatham House, says that "it's not clear whether Putin would meet Trump and Zelensky", adding that "meeting Zelensky is the last thing that Putin would be prepared to do".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump exploits France riots to push false immigration claims ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adda69676c0076cd346a9ff0feed6356a4b02688f203ef114d9e26e24e90831f</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump and his inner circle are using unrest in France to push unsubstantiated claims blaming the riots on immigration, even showing French protest footage at midterm rallies. But there is no evidence linking immigration to the unrest, and it's prompted French President Emmanuel Macron to accuse world leaders of making “stupid comments” at France’s expense. Trump’s focus comes as Republicans face mounting pressure ahead of the midterms and his approval rating hits a reported record low.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Neither the Sudanese military, nor the RSF take any acknowledgement of human life in this war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8383eaf5d5f8a9e6fa61a72cb523c314d8b82146eedf7cb9a71a3b502e5667ee</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war" /><summary type="html">The death toll from a drone strike Monday on a market in an area disputed between Sudan and South Sudan has risen to 153 and is likely even higher, a local official told AFP on Wednesday. Authorities in Abyei district said the strike on the Amiet market involved the use of multiple munitions and was carried out by the Sudanese army. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Jan Pospisil, Sudan Affairs Analyst at the Peace and Conflict Resolution Evidence Platform. He says that for a long time the Sudanese army has tried "to portray a picture internationally that they are humane, whereas RSF is committing atrocities. Here we see very clearly that there is not much difference between these two".</summary></entry><entry><title>Le Pen sees polls boost amid mass protests, riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:996e4173a0d4cc6cbbc7e1827122ef90e4ee4c4f7bd4dc20332a3fb1375066e4</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T18:56:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/le-pen-sees-polls-boost-amid-mass-protests-riots" /><summary type="html">Marine Le Pen is set to officially launch her presidential campaign this weekend at the National Rally two-day party congress in Orléans. The latest Ifop poll, carried out in the wake of the mass protests and riots in France, suggests the far right leader would win the first round of the presidential election by a wide margin, and far-left candidate Jean-Luc Melenchon emerged as her most likely opponent in the runoff. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump faces fresh questions over ties to 'humanitarian' Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fee72e0e5e8a92e781226757bd72bb5dde0df67629d86cb25f26983b43f3a28f</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T18:53:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-faces-fresh-questions-over-ties-to-humanitarian-putin" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's pivot away from Ukraine has triggered fresh questions about his attachment to Russian leader Vladimir Putin, the man a top American envoy flattered on Wednesday as a "humanitarian. Trump has cast his dealings with Putin as part of a mega-deal that has secured the release of American detainee Stephen Hubbard -- and which Trump says will end Russia's war on Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kharkiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canadian publisher drops author Orelien after confirming he used AI in debut novel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b56a0465b91e1cab87682c788261d7c03eaf09de69cdce2ebbf01cdc43bd41f0</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T17:32:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20261021-canadian-publisher-drops-author-orelien-after-confirming-he-used-ai-in-debut-novel" /><summary type="html">The Canadian publisher representing Thélyson Orélien on Wednesday said it had dropped the prize-nominated writer over new information indicating that he did use artificial intelligence to write his acclaimed debut.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Riyadh to show solidarity amid Houthi attacks, ease tensions at home via fuel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3e9719d97d25d245340297d4c0ca8cef86d151df1a04f085176d9a41b86ea48</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T17:09:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/macron-visits-riyadh-show-solidarity-amid-houthi-attacks-ease-tensions-home-via-fuel-deal" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Wednesday paid an unannounced visit to Riyadh in a bid to underscore French support for the kingdom amid intensified attacks by Houthi rebels and an attempt to ease tensions at home by securing oil and diesel imports.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Greece: Protesters draw inspiration from demonstrations in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a0b9a68a7925ed0b9eafe02a03e2bba1b7ee74f226e9f516211da48f79e1d55</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:31:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-greece-protesters-draw-inspiration-from-demonstrations-in-france" /><summary type="html">Inspired by protests in France and other parts of Europe, thousands of Greek students on Wednesday demonstrated around the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>World set to breach 1.5°C warming limit set by Paris Climate Agreement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64684a20cff4eda008468a33b27c5a060aae995d7e229aec2508c100a1aaffb2</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:56:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-world-set-to-breach-1-5%C2%B0c-warming-limit-set-by-paris-climate-agreement" /><summary type="html">The UN is warning that global commitments to cut planet-heating emissions are falling far short of the Paris climate goals of 1.5 degrees Celsius warming – and put the world on course for 2.6C warming this century. The report by the United Nations Environment Programme lays bare the chasm between rhetoric and action when it comes to tackling global warming, and the challenge before political leaders at November's COP31 climate summit - set to take place next month in Turkey. Story by Emerald Maxwell.</summary></entry><entry><title>French President Macron lands in Saudi Arabia on surprise 'solidarity' visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:248d125dd7475e51b7fea0872c19cd54bd4772d8b52c09396ba3233c0cb1b518</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-president-macron-lands-in-saudi-arabia-on-surprise-solidarity-visit" /><summary type="html">⁠French President Emmanuel ​Macron landed in Riyadh on Wednseday, ‌adding an ⁠unscheduled stop to his ‌ongoing tour of the Gulf ⁠region. The president's office said the visit aimed to demonstrate “France's solidarity” ​with Saudi Arabia in ‌the face of attacks launched by the ‌Houthis against its territory. Details by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Douglas Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says 'ready' to resume 3-way talks with US and Ukraine mid-November</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b047110d8b4fece8ead8945869c5765e8c31299bde7d145727eef726843e25a</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:51:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kremlin-says-ready-to-resume-3-way-talks-with-us-and-ukraine-mid-november" /><summary type="html">Moscow is ready to resume trilateral US-Ukraine-Russia talks next month, the Kremlin said Wednesday after President Vladimir Putin met with US envoy Steve Witkoff in Russia. FRANCE 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron rejects Trump’s claims blaming migrants for French riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01d65ed63472bb8001b3bfb8841d4e0dc2ff15d68f1c1f039578c95de7ce9be9</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-macron-rejects-trump-s-claims-blaming-migrants-for-french-riots" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron condemned comments by "foreign leaders" on the violent protests in France on October 17. He has now arrived in Saudi Arabia as part of his Gulf tour.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Far right leader Marine Le Pen gains popularity amid nationwide riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cecd77bb4874cb9b328c387b9b1de38d37c24d1ae6f9d4d6be4539e8a78e688f</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:29:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-far-right-leader-marine-le-pen-gains-popularity-amid-nationwide-riots" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu met with union leaders today in France. His government admitted law enforcement officers had lost control this past weekend during protests which resulted in scenes of violence and looting. The country is bracing for more protests – the Yellow Vest movement called on demonstrators to take to the street on Saturday. As the events unfold, far-right leader Marine Le Pen is gaining popularity. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi.</summary></entry><entry><title>Some Brazilians long associated with the left now shift towards Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79a4c3c52b3ca118561bf462e6586d2aaeaa49588bb158211716d73ec0484722</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-some-brazilians-long-associated-with-the-left-now-shift-towards-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">In the first round of Brazil’s presidential elections, Flavio Bolsonaro got the most votes in 15 electoral districts in the North Zone of Rio de Janeiro, compared with 9 for Lula. This part of the city, long associated with the left and the social policies of Lula’s Workers’ Party, is now shifting towards former president Jair Bolsonaro’s son.</summary></entry><entry><title>70% of water produced in Guadeloupe never reaches homes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64a2e67c48b6aa28b4e782b50cec42b6990c35577c1be1dbba35c36bed99059b</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:26:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261021-70-of-water-produced-in-guadeloupe-never-reaches-homes" /><summary type="html">In the French overseas territory of Guadeloupe, a water crisis is a daily reality, with some residents going without water for weeks. The network is being repaired, but at the current pace, France's Court of Auditors says replacing all of it would take 208 years. Now, a judicial investigation has been opened in Paris into the crisis, following a citizen-led legal action. Our France 2 colleagues report.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Italy: Giorgia Meloni approves tougher anti-riot laws after Milan violence 🇮🇹</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9efb51e2379b331bd0968bdc7dbad9386adcfa6f0157d755fe1b8fc886f0a225</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:18:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-italy-giorgia-meloni-approves-tougher-anti-riot-laws-after-milan-violence-%F0%9F%87%AE%F0%9F%87%B9" /><summary type="html">Italy approved a raft of security measures on Tuesday including a new offence of violent participation in a demonstration, tougher penalties for rioters, and financial liability for parents whose children take part in vandalism and looting.</summary></entry><entry><title>Prosecutors search European Parliament offices of far-right Patriots bloc in graft probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef4a0103c90c6f612bc7bba455cb2bf1b986815a8a6dd3f7795d5cdcedfcaef7</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:07:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-prosecutors-search-european-parliament-offices-of-far-right-patriots-bloc-in-graft-probe" /><summary type="html">EU prosecutors on Wednesday searched offices belonging to the far-right Patriots parliamentary group as part of a graft probe into the bloc’s dissolved predecessor, Identity and Democracy, which brought together several European far-right parties including French presidential candidate Marine Le Pen’s National Rally.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Film show: Olivia Colman, Alexander Skarsgård star in horny feminist fantasy 'Wicker'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4094f14bbb53497ef6c3850292753fd0accd2f05f75c0926d9786e8aff0ca8d3</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:54:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261021-film-show-olivia-colman-alexander-skarsg%C3%A5rd-star-in-horny-feminist-fantasy-wicker" /><summary type="html">Film critic Emma Jones and Dheepthika Laurent discuss the week's film releases. Olivia Colman and Alexander Skarsgård play an odd couple in the fantasy romance "Wicker" about love, society and the patriarchy.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia both ready to resume trilateral talks with US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a78cca7824cd7e3f9c65e39c5e21743523f77c866f3fdcb6a33f3717822b0ae1</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:46:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-zelensky-proposes-freezing-front-with-russia-first-step-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Russia on Wednesday said they are both ready to resume trilateral talks with the United States. The news comes after US envoy Steve Witkoff separately met with Volodymyr Zelensky and Vladimir Putin on two consecutive days.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Peter Zalmayev: 'Ukraine was showing all sorts of cards that Trump took away and gave to Putin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3c43aa1c27a15a65202edc0b0107625cc0a88bbed5f94836b40db473d674755</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:44:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin-1" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. And he warns, "I'm seeing, I'm smelling a Yalta II. I'm smelling another Munich (1938), where we're seeing appeasement of the aggressor." Ukraine faces the possibility that its sovereignty and security could become mere bargaining chips in an era Zalmayev describes as great-power "collusion". He delivers a forceful critique of the Trump administration's approach to Russia, arguing that Washington is weakening Ukraine's negotiating position while offering Vladimir Putin little incentive to abandon his maximalist demands. At stake, he suggests, are the cohesion of the transatlantic alliance, and the credibility of Western security commitments.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pain au Chocolat: The sweet story behind a French breakfast icon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56b2d1ca9da8a60ad15956d218d0b75c5a4ff0cfe3ad5b5dfb9cbd8280462f20</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:32:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pain-au-chocolat-the-sweet-story-behind-a-french-breakfast-icon" /><summary type="html">Did you know French people eat 1.4 billion pain au chocolats a year. The sweet treat is a national treasure, but a debate rages on over what to call it.</summary></entry><entry><title>France braces for another weekend of protests amid nationwide riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96896909665f3f935206355665c8cd26fe7507f233d98dddb6bbed2077d50dc4</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:27:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-another-weekend-of-protests-amid-nationwide-riots" /><summary type="html">France is bracing for yet another weekend of protests by high school students and the "Yellow Vest" movement. The government says they're increasing security and personnel to trying to mitigate any violence or chaos. Story by Ophelie Jacobson and France 2.</summary></entry><entry><title>Greece: Protesters demand increased funding for public education</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42a4f80706260af92a9e89e22ae1b5e2722bb96494fdeb7a2ba46d51a59995ea</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:25:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/greece-protesters-demand-increased-funding-for-public-education" /><summary type="html">Students, teachers and civil servants are demonstrating in Greece today, protesting over staff shortages, poor infrastructure and the cost of living. Dozens of students have set up tents in the Square facing Parliament, in Athens, and on a pedestrian street in Thessaloniki on Tuesday. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Athens, Nathalie Savaricas.</summary></entry><entry><title>'I didn’t know it was theft': Trials begin in Paris following October 17 violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ede8e2200670c1c6e70ca8dd0953b01f55bd832dfc7d3f2abc861ce132f940ee</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:15:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261021-i-didn-t-know-it-was-theft-trials-begin-paris-following-october-17-violence" /><summary type="html">Those arrested during the October 17 rallies filed into the dock at Paris’s Judicial Court on Tuesday, accused of a broad range of offences – from assault against police officers to resisting arrest and handling stolen goods. The courtroom’s charged atmosphere was palpable amid the justice minister’s call for the law to respond with “utmost firmness”.</summary><category term="France" /></entry></feed>
